From 52e5694f4136b34e12e5e7997949bbc63430cbba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ismail Ramzi <ismail@bugqore.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 16:03:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] unexpand: fix heap overflow on negative-width whitespace

* src/unexpand.c (unexpand): Clamp a negative c32width() to 1 when
accumulating a blank, matching the sibling non-blank path and expand
and fold.  A separator whose display width is negative (e.g. U+0085
where c32issep() accepts it) left 'column' un-advanced, so the pending
blank buffer, sized for one byte of advance per blank, grew without
bound.
* NEWS: Mention the bug fix.

Link: https://github.com/coreutils/coreutils/pull/361
---
diff --git a/src/unexpand.c b/src/unexpand.c
index 6a9881c215..630be36135 100644
--- a/src/unexpand.c
+++ b/src/unexpand.c
@@ -199,7 +199,8 @@ unexpand (void)
                         }
                       else
                         {
-                          column += c32width (g.ch);
+                          int width = c32width (g.ch);
+                          column += width < 0 ? 1 : width;
 
                           if (! (prev_blank && column >= next_tab_column))
                             {
